Can one room host all the meetings? Sort by start time, then walk adjacent pairs: if any meeting starts before the previous one ends, a conflict exists and the answer is no.

```python
def can_attend_all(meetings):
    meetings.sort(key=lambda m: m[0])
    for i in range(1, len(meetings)):
        if meetings[i][0] < meetings[i - 1][1]:
            return False
    return True
```

This only needs to check **adjacent** pairs in sorted order — if meeting i doesn't overlap meeting i-1, it can't overlap anything even earlier either, since starts only increase. It's O(n log n), dominated by the sort, same shape as the overlap check inside Merge Intervals.
